<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Vietnamese (vi) for :core:ui. Mirrors values/strings.xml key for key.

  WORDING BAN (LLM.md §1, §5) carries into every locale, not only English: nothing below claims to
  remove a virus, block a scam, speed a phone up or free memory, and no string carries a performance
  percentage. The security feature keeps the owner's framing, "kiểm tra an toàn ứng dụng".

  PLURALS — Vietnamese has ONE CLDR plural category, `other`. A `one` item here would never be
  selected and lint flags it (UnusedQuantity), so the plural bodies below carry `other` alone. The
  count still goes through <plurals> rather than a hand-built string, which is the rule the English
  file states.
-->
